{% comment %}
  The top of every ordinary page: the title in the middle with the OCP arrow
  set at its upper left, pointing down into the word, and a paragraph of
  introduction under it. One section so every page opens the same way —
  locations, about, contact, a collection and whatever comes next.

  The title falls back to whichever resource the template is for — a page's
  own title, or a collection's — so a fresh page or a new collection needs
  nothing typed here. `/collections/all` is the one exception: every
  collection uses this same template, so its title can't be set per
  collection in the template JSON the way `page.json`'s can, and Shopify's
  own title for that virtual collection ("All products") isn't what a
  merchant typically wants read out here — so it's the one case with its own
  setting instead of just reading `collection.title`.

  The introduction does not fall back to the page's body: that is long on
  some pages (policies), and would land the whole thing up here.

  Not a `{% doc %}`: those are not valid in sections.
{% endcomment %}

{% liquid
  assign title = section.settings.title
  if title == blank
    if page != blank
      assign title = page.title
    elsif collection != blank
      if collection.handle == 'all'
        assign title = section.settings.all_products_title | default: 'Products'
      else
        assign title = collection.title
      endif
    endif
  endif
  assign heading_font = section.settings.heading_font | default: 'heading'
%}

<header
  class="page-hero"
  style="
    --page-hero-font: var(--font-{{ heading_font }}--family);
    --page-hero-weight: var(--font-{{ heading_font }}--weight);
  "
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <h1 class="page-hero__title">
    {%- if section.settings.show_arrow -%}
      <span class="page-hero__mark" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'logo-arrow' %}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
    <span class="page-hero__title-text">{{ title }}</span>
  </h1>

  {%- if section.settings.description != blank -%}
    <div class="page-hero__description rte">{{ section.settings.description }}</div>
  {%- endif -%}
</header>

{% stylesheet %}
  .page-hero {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding: 5rem var(--ocp-page-margin) 4rem;
    text-align: center;
    background: var(--color-background);
    color: var(--color-foreground);
  }

  /*
   * A row, not centred text with something hung off it: the arrow and the
   * word are laid out side by side and the pair is centred on the page as
   * one unit, matching the Figma frame (a 217×47 auto-layout row, itself
   * centred, holding a 21×21 arrow then the word with a 4px gap). Sizes
   * below are that frame's own ratios against its 36px type — 21/36 for the
   * arrow, 4/36 for the gap — kept in em so both scale with the title
   * wherever its actual size ends up (this page's is not fixed at 36px).
   *
   * `align-items: flex-start` is the row-level equivalent of the Figma
   * frame's nested layout, where the arrow sits inside its own column
   * top-aligned against the row's full height: the word's own box is taller
   * than the arrow (line-height above 1), so top-aligning both is what
   * lets the arrow read as sitting slightly above the word instead of
   * centred through its middle.
   */
  .page-hero__title {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.11em;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--page-hero-font);
    font-weight: var(--page-hero-weight);
    font-size: var(--ocp-display-size-sm);
    line-height: var(--ocp-leading-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--ocp-letter-spacing);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .page-hero__mark {
    flex: none;
    width: 0.58em;
  }

  .page-hero__mark svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /*
   * The mark is a single filled shape with no weight axis of its own — a
   * stroke in the same colour fattens its edges outward, same trick as a
   * faux-bold. Width is in the path's own 215-unit viewBox, not CSS px, so
   * it scales with the mark's size rather than needing its own unit.
   *
   * Its corners were never the problem — every angle in this path is 45°
   * or wider, well inside what even the default miter limit (4) renders as
   * a sharp point. The earlier attempt at this raised the limit anyway,
   * which did nothing, because the actual cause was the stroke-width
   * itself: the diagonal arm this path traces is only ~19.6 units wide at
   * its narrowest, and a stroke of 12 (added to both sides of the line)
   * fattened it past that — the two edges' strokes met and overlapped
   * inside the point, and the overlap is what rendered as a soft, rounded
   * blob rather than a crisp tip. Kept well under half that width instead.
   */
  .page-hero__mark svg path {
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 5;
    stroke-linejoin: miter;
  }

  .page-hero__description {
    max-width: 40rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body--family);
    font-size: var(--ocp-text-size);
    line-height: var(--ocp-leading-text);
    letter-spacing: var(--ocp-letter-spacing);
  }

  .page-hero__description > :first-child {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }

  .page-hero__description > :last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Page hero",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "title",
      "label": "Title",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the page's or collection's own title."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "all_products_title",
      "label": "Title for the \"All\" collection",
      "info": "Every collection shares this template, so this is the one collection whose title needs its own setting rather than just reading the collection's own name.",
      "default": "Products"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_arrow",
      "label": "Arrow beside the title",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "description",
      "label": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "heading_font",
      "label": "Title font",
      "options": [
        { "value": "body", "label": "Body" },
        { "value": "subheading", "label": "Subheading" },
        { "value": "heading", "label": "Heading" },
        { "value": "accent", "label": "Accent" }
      ],
      "default": "heading"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Page hero"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
